Implemented a self-contained Track B generator for the paper’s native polymatrix-game setting:

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2112.03442/gen_2112_03442.py:35)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2112.03442/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2112.03442/README.md)
- [Oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2112.03442/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2112.03442/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2112.03442/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The module inverse-generates sparse, exact mixed Nash equilibria disguised by Walsh–Hadamard systems. All local gates pass:

- G4: 0/200,000 guesses in an 80-bit structure-aware space
- G6: four attacks at 0/8; reference and compact solvers both 8/8
- G8: 120/120 invariance checks
- G9(c): 165 characters, 24 atoms, 165 intended operations
- Independent exact check: 40,960/40,960 players indifferent

It is not submission-ready: the preliminary easy oracle rung was solved 2/3, then OpenRouter exhausted its key limit at medium. No hardness verdict or current G9 arms could be obtained, and the 403 errors were not counted as failures. A replenished `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` is required to rerun STEP 4 and the two G9 diagnostics.
